# S12 BTM roadmap v3 critique — owner queue assessment (16 open judgments)

Run: `Tasks/critique-machinery/runs/claude-seat-s12-btm-page-v3` (first critique of the version 3
page; 60 Claude seat readings, 60 valid, 180 applicable cells recorded, 163 agreed — 159 clear and
4 defects — 16 seat disagreements, and 1 recording refusal). Prepared by Claude, 2026-09-04, for
Kamen's ruling. Every recommendation is one of the offered verdicts (`reject` / `revise` / `clear`)
and rests on words on the delivered page, in its stored payload, or in its registered producer
pages — never on the seats' reasoning alone (the seats return a verdict and a line span).

Recording plan on approval: each ruling is filed with `answer-owner` as
"Kamen: approved in bulk 2026-09-04 — reasoning drafted by Claude, adopted by the owner:
<the grounding below>".

Comparison with the version 2 critique (same seats, same lenses): applicable cells 144 → 180
(six more units on the longer page); agreed defects 7 → 4; disagreements 14 → 16; revise cells
after rulings 15 → 9 if the recommendations below are adopted. None of the fifteen cells closed in
round 2 came back: the doors, the approve door, the map spans, the advocates and the KPI measures
all read clear or are disputed on new grounds.

